message.content:
Teddy bears are classified in heading 9503.00 as toys representing animals or non-human creatures. Stuffed toys fall under subheading 9503.00.00, with the 10-digit statistical suffixes under HTSUS as follows: 9503.00.0073 is "Stuffed toys representing animals or non-human creatures," and 9503.00.0071 is "Other: Toys representing animals…, stuffed" (older). The current structure has 9503.00.0073 as "Other toys; ... Stuffed toys," described as "Toys representing animals or non-human creatures (for example, robots and monsters) and parts and accessories thereof: Stuffed."

The code for stuffed toys representing animals is 9503.00.0073 (US Note, "Other"). I am fairly confident of that code.

{"hts_code": "9503.00.0073", "reason": "A plush stuffed teddy bear is a stuffed toy representing an animal, classified in heading 9503 despite its awareness-promoting theme."}
